# ============================================================================
# Clubset environment configuration
# ============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values from your Supabase project settings
# (Project Settings -> API).
#
# The publishable key is designed to be public. It is safe in the browser ONLY because
# every table in this schema has Row Level Security enabled and every RPC
# re-checks permissions server-side (PRD 41). Never put the service_role key in
# a VITE_ variable -- anything prefixed VITE_ ships to the browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Turnstile site key. Public by design -- it ships in the browser
# bundle, exactly like the Supabase publishable key above.
#
# Leave this line absent to use the checked-in fallback site key. Set it to an
# empty value ONLY if CAPTCHA is also disabled in Supabase Auth; otherwise the
# widget renders nothing, no token is produced, and every protected auth call
# fails closed with "captcha_failed".
#
# The matching SECRET key belongs in Supabase Auth -> Bot and Abuse Protection,
# which verifies tokens server-side. Never put it in this file, in a VITE_
# variable, or in the Vercel/Cloudflare environment.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: exact extra origins that auth emails may return to, comma
# separated. Production always returns to https://clubset.vercel.app.
#
# Set this only for a local or preview origin that is ALSO on the Supabase
# Auth redirect allow-list. The value must be the exact origin, never a
# wildcard and never anything user-supplied. Supabase falls back to its Site
# URL (currently the obsolete Joinin domain) for anything it does not list.
#
# The hosted project currently allows http://127.0.0.1:8080 but NOT
# http://localhost:8080.
# VITE_AUTH_REDIRECT_ORIGINS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server / CLI only. NEVER prefix these with VITE_ and never commit .env.
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY are the non-VITE fallbacks read by
# src/integrations/supabase/client.ts when the VITE_ variants are absent (SSR).
# They are public client configuration, but they are also consumed server-side,
# so they may live in .env without a VITE_ prefix.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is the privileged server-only credential used by
# src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts (supabaseAdmin). It bypasses RLS,
# so it MUST remain server-only: never prefix with VITE_, never ship to the
# browser, never return it in an API response, never log it, never commit it.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN is a management-API token for the Supabase CLI. It can
# read and change the whole project, so it must live only in the local,
# git-ignored .env (or an OS keyring) -- never in the repository, a migration,
# a VITE_ variable, or an agent config file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
